{"text": "Philip Morris U.S.A.\nCONFIDENTIAL\nC.1. HIGHLIGHTS\n\nJULY, 1994\n\nRJ. REYNOLDS\nBRENTWOOD\n\nR. J. Reynolds is manufacturing ten packings of Brentwood cigarettes. This discount product is distributed by\nForsyth Tobacco Products, Winston-Salem, NC, and is available in Revco stores only. The blend of Brentwood\nis similar to that of Monarch and Best Value. The cigarettes tested were March production, and were purchased\nin Virginia.\n\nTar, Nicotine, Menthol,\nFull Flavor KS (SP) 13 o7 -\nFull Flavor Menthol KS (SP) 1S 08 Os\nFull Flavor 100 (SP) 13 07 -\nFull Flavor Menthol 100 (SP) 13 07 04\nLights KS (SP) 9 Os -\nLights Menthol KS (SP) 9 0.6 04\nLights 100 (SP) 9 06 -\nLights Menthol 100 (SP) 9 0.6 0.5\nUltra Lights KS (SP) 4 03 -\nUltra Lights 100 (SP) 5 03 -\nBRAND MODIFICATIONS.\nR.J. REYNOLDS\nMONARCH\nBEST VALUE\n\nReynolds increased the level of expanded tobacco (26 to 32%) in March production Monarch and Best Value.\nThe results were reported in the June Highlights. At that time, lower tobacco weight and rod density were\n\u2018observed for Monarch and Best Value Full Flavor KS, Monarch Lights Menthol KS, and Monarch Lights 100.\nReductions in tobacco weight and rod density were observed for the following brands in May production:\n\u2018Monarch Full Flavor Menthol KS, Monarch Full Flavor 100, Monarch Lights KS, Monarch Lights Menthol 100,\n\u2018Monarch Ultra Lights 100, Best Value Full Flavor 100, Best Value Lights 100 (Plain & Menthol), and Best\nValue Ultra Lights 100.\n\nR.J. REYNOLDS:\n\nWINSTON SELECT LIGHTS KS (SP)\n\nHigher tar (10.5 to 12.4 mg/cigt.) and nicotine (0.79 to 0.96 mg/cigt.) deliveries were observed for Winston\nSelect Lights KS cigarettes, correlating with the change to a less permeable cigarette paper (45 to 36 CORESTA\nUnits). The higher nicotine delivery also correlated with a higher level of total alkaloids (1.88 to 2.04%).\n\nDOC CODE: POs22 2\n\n2TETLE ESOS",
